// __fern_tcp_connect_with(addr, port, nonblocking) is a socket connected
// to addr:port (4 or 16 network-order bytes), or -errno with the socket
// closed again. With `nonblocking` (the builtin's boolean, an i32 here)
// the socket is non-blocking and the connect is only started: the
// descriptor comes back while it is under way, and control op 5 reports
// how it ended.
